    "notes": "Margaret inherited Hainaut, Holland and Zeeland after William II's childless death. Her marriage to Emperor Louis IV carried the inheritance into the Wittelsbach dynasty; after conflict with her son William, she retained Hainaut until her death in 1356. The requested name 'Margaret I of Hainaut' is potentially misleading. She is normally Margaret II of Hainaut but Margaret I of Holland. The Wittelsbach successor in Hainaut in 1356 was her son William III of Hainaut (1330–1389), not Albert I. William III is missing from the requested 15-person list and must not be replaced by a fictional direct Margaret-to-Albert succession.",
